{"name":"Dame Dignity","hex":"#999ba8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dame","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Usually capitalized as Dame: a title equivalent to Sir for a female knight.","A matron at a school, especially Eton College."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a dame."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dame"},{"term":"dignity","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being dignified or worthy of esteem: elevation of mind or character.","Decorum, formality, stateliness. (Discuss this sense)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dignity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dame","blocks":[{"text":"Dame is a traditionally British honorific title given to women who have been admitted to certain orders of chivalry. It is the female equivalent of Sir, the title used by knights. Baronetesses in their own right also use the title Dame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Dame2022.jpg/330px-Dame2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dame","wikidata":"Q901407"},{"title":"Dignity","blocks":[{"text":"Dignity is the right of a person to be valued and respected for their own sake, and to be treated ethically. In this context, it is of significance in morality, ethics, law and politics as an extension of the Enlightenment-era concepts of inherent, inalienable rights. The term may also be used to describe personal conduct, as in \"behaving with dignity\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dignity","wikidata":"Q274782"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg/500px-Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg/500px-Ripa_dignity_allegory_%287885027%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Woodcut from Cesare Ripa's Iconologia depicting the Allegory of Dignity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARipa_dignity_allegory_(7885027).jpg"}],"sounds":{"dame":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/En-au-dame.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c6/En-au-dame.ogg/En-au-dame.ogg.mp3"}],"dignity":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5f/En-us-dignity.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5f/En-us-dignity.ogg/En-us-dignity.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey Bushchat in Sillery Gaon March 2025 by Tisha Mukherjee 01","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg/500px-Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg","ratio":1.3997488488907492,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_Bushchat_in_Sillery_Gaon_March_2025_by_Tisha_Mukherjee_01.jpg","share":0.494375},{"title":"Scala di grigi","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Scala_di_grigi.jpg/500px-Scala_di_grigi.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scala_di_grigi.jpg","share":0.304375},{"title":"Madeira Grey Cat","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Madeira_Grey_Cat.JPG/500px-Madeira_Grey_Cat.JPG","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madeira_Grey_Cat.JPG","share":0.27625},{"title":"Grey rectangle","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Grey_rectangle.jpg/500px-Grey_r